WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
Pick one carbon atom in your arm.

2
00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:04.720
Yesterday, it was in your lunch.

3
00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.180
Before that, it was in a wheat plant.

4
00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:10.770
And before that, it was
carbon dioxide in the air.

5
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.470
Some carbon stays put far longer.

6
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.930
Plant remains became peat, and
over millions of years, coal.

7
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:22.760
So how do carbon atoms keep moving
between the air and living things?

8
00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.970
In this mission, you'll
map where carbon is stored:

9
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:30.460
the air, the oceans, living
things, rocks and fuels.

10
00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:34.080
Then you'll see how slow
stores, like coal and limestone,

11
00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.970
hold carbon for millions of years.

12
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.660
Your mission: find out how carbon atoms
keep moving between the air and living

13
00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:42.450
things.
